==Official Introduction==
> Zani, a serious and reliable Montelli employee, follows a strict routine and manages tasks with ease.

For years, she has clocked in on time without fail, finding as much enjoyment in her well-ordered life as in her carefully planned moments of leisure.
> — Description from the [https://wutheringwaves.kurogames.com/en/main#resonators Official Website] 

==Personality==
Zani has a fascinating duality of character: a fastidiously well-ordered and extremely competent professional during the day, and a powerful, nearly elemental, force for justice at night. Her public image is one of steadfast devotion to routine and order, a quality she nurtures through her decades-long association with the [[Montelli Family|Montelli family]]'s [[Averardo Bank]]. She is a disciplined professional in the way she goes about her job, and her penchant for an ordered existence extends even to her personal habits and tastes, including her desire for comfort foods at the end of a long day. Despite her obvious professionalism, she often expresses a dry, matter-of-fact weariness with her work, viewing it as a part of her existence that is inevitable, if not always welcome, and looking at inefficiency or busywork with a practical disdain. Her secret history as the "Blazing Nightwalker" tells of a deep-seated sense of justice beyond the law.

Zani dismantled a reigning criminal syndicate one-handed in this covert identity, becoming a vigilante when the established channels were useless. Her motives are not narcissistic or fueled by the desire to be famous; indeed, she finds her heroic moniker "ridiculous" and actively avoids the limelight, understanding that fame gets in the way of her job. This is a pragmatic choice, as it allows her to pursue justice without targeting herself. But this past has had a lasting effect. 

Zani carries a subtle exhaustion that she tends to express as insomnia, a testament to the heavy toll of what she has endured. She is not very forthcoming about much, but she is quite candid about the fact that this vigorous vigilante work "changed her", causing a "lost spark" and a crushing exhaustion. Despite this personal cost, her internal drive to protect the innocent and bring order is steadfast. Her mental strength is amazing, channeling her stress into positive, albeit unconventional, outlets. Joining the Montelli family was a tactical decision, offering structure and resources to help her continue her mission of bringing order and tidying up the residual chaos of her own activities. Zani is defined by her powers of observation, analytical nature, and quick wit in her interactions.

Her dry sarcasm and understated humor are favorite devices that she uses both as a defense and to communicate her special point of view. Zani is fiercely loyal to those she trusts and to the Montellis, always putting their interests first. This loyalty is balanced, however, by a strong moral compass; she doesn't shy away from navigating dangerous political waters or taking on corruption when it gets in the way of justice. Her ability to read situations quickly, connect seemingly unrelated clues, and act swiftly wins her a worthwhile ally. Not overtly emotional, Zani possesses a strong, if unassuming, sense of compassion.

She keeps a small, cherished doll, a gift from one of the children she rescued, as a quiet, personal reminder of the worth of her work and the true motivation for her to carry on her fight. Zani has a protective instinct for others, particularly those near and dear to her, and is constantly advising them to rest and not fall into the trap of doing too much, drawing on her own experience. She values integrity and open-mindedness in others, even in members of the opposing factions, and is not averse to forming alliances when there are common goals to be pursued. Zani's journey is one of grappling with the tension between her natural preference for order and her strong, almost primal, need for immediate action.

Zani dreams of a peaceful, secure [[Ragunna City|Ragunna]] where every individual can find his or her niche, a dream inextricably tied to her sense of belonging to her hometown. The introduction of new issues, and particularly her meetings with the [[Rover]], seem to bring a new sense of direction and a "burst of color" into her otherwise highly regulated life. She recognizes the Rover's unique capacity for positive change, even going so far as to admit that their presence might render her own vigilante function "increasingly irrelevant" - a development she welcomes, as it brings her one step closer to the quiet, peaceful life she secretly desires. Her fondest wish, after all, is for a world peaceful enough that she can finally "sleep through the night", undisturbed by the constant fight for justice. She is a testament to unlimited potential, understated resilience, and an unwavering, if often concealed, dedication to a greater, more orderly world. 

==Appearance==
Zani is a tall woman with pale skin, white hair, and dark red eyes with slitted pupils. She has a distinct beauty mark under her right eye, as well as dark eyebags. Due to her awakening, she now has black, ram-like horns and a slim tail with a pointed tip.

===Clothing===
Zani wears a high collared white button-up shirt with cuffed sleeves that reach past her elbows and has golden buttons. She wears a bright red tie atop her shirt, along with a black leather harness that goes above her chest and hooks over her right shoulder, clasped with a circular golden buckle. Beneath her shirt collar is a frilled collar as well as a black choker that matches her harness, the pouch on her right bicep contains a radio, and she wears a black arm band around her left bicep bearing the Montelli family sigil. The lower half of her outfit consists of tight black high-waist pants with golden zips on each leg ending mid-way down her thighs. 

Among her other accessories are a golden pair of key-shaped earrings with green gems, as well as black half-palm leather gloves. She wears red socks and a pair of strapless black high heels with red soles.

When using her [[Forte]], Zani's outfit changes, mostly the upper half. Her shirt becomes ripped, with the sleeves ending before her shoulders and a low-cut V-shaped collar that dips halfway down her chest. The back of her shirt is completely torn, with the cut going all the way down and showing her [[Tacet Mark]] located on her back. She loosely wraps her tie around her right arm and wears two thin black bands on both her biceps. Her black choker stays but is adorned with golden horizontal stripes that match her horns and the golden scars on her body. The lower half of her outfit stays the same as it does in her regular form. The vents on her horns also glow a bright yellow.

